MultiportRouter draws a router table as a multiport valve in plan: the valve in the middle with one numbered port per situation, each port piped to its route card, the chosen card lit steel blue and the valve's lever turned to its port.

- On the site: a `table` block with `as: "router"` and `"look": "multiport-router"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-multiport-router.js`), on ind-personal-care "Start from your situation". Concept: pass 12 image 196 (`design-system/inspiration/gemini/196-p12-ind-personal-care-start.png`); only the idea is taken (valve, numbered ports, pipes to cards, one card lit), never its words.
- Markup: `div.aq-multiport-router` (grid: cards left, valve, cards right; `--m` rows) → `div.__plant` (`svg.__valve`: body, rings, port bosses and their PP true-union ends (`__union`: two 3 px rings and a hex nut), `__pn` port numbers, `__mark` position marks, `g.__lever` turned by `--a`), `svg.__pipes` (drawn by the renderer in the block's own pixels: per route `g.__pipe` with `__wall`, `__bore`, `__water`), `ol.__routes[data-pk-picker="chips"]` of `li.__route[data-pk-item]` → `button.__chip[data-pk-head]` (phones) and `article.__card[data-pk-body]` (`__no` "01 /", `h3.__sit[data-pk-desk]` holding `button.__pick` with `aria-pressed`, `dl.__dl` of the remaining columns; the start-with cell `.is-go`).
- Fields: as Router: `cols`, `rows` (cells strings or `{t, link, intent}`). No new fields. Ports alternate left and right (01 top left, 02 top right …), so two to eight routes.
- Choosing: a click anywhere on a card (not its link) or on its title button chooses it; the lever turns (CSS 500 ms), the pipe's bore fills with `flow`, the card takes `flow-tint` with a `flow` edge, the port number turns `flow`. The first route is chosen on load.
- Tokens: paper ground, valve in `ink` lines on `surface-raised`, lever `ink` with a `surface-raised` nut and `surface-sunken` grip (near navy in light, light in dark; `navy` was 1.26:1 on the dark valve face), pipes `line-strong` twin wall, the chosen route `flow`. Card titles Geist 22/28; labels mono 12 px uppercase; start-with link at least 44 px.
- **Phones** (`@container` ≤ 860 px, PhoneKit chips, one column): a 168 px valve on a riser (flow) heads the block over a header rule; the situations are 48 px chips (15 px text, number in mono), the chosen chip filled `flow`; its card opens under the chips with the need and a 48 px start-with row link; the lever follows the chip (`pk:change`). Without script every card shows, titled. About 880 px tall for four routes (decision-valve was 1,630).
- Use it for two to eight exclusive situations, each leading to one start page. For many situations or a long answer per situation, use StairRouter or Router.

## Motion

On scroll-in the valve rises in, the pipes run out from its ports to the cards (DrawSVG on wall and bore), the chosen pipe fills, the cards follow and the lever swings from rest to port 01. Each later choice runs the water along the chosen pipe again (0.45 s). Once, under 3 s; nothing under reduced motion (the lever still turns by CSS). Phones: valve and chips rise in.
